ust load the installed graphify skill before any other action, so the canonical workflow is followed rather than ad-hoc exploration.","source_file":"AGENTS.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"id":"agents_graphify_wiki_navigation","label":"Graphify Wiki Index Navigation","_origin":"semantic","author":null,"captured_at":null,"community":2,"community_name":"Graphify Agent Workflow","contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","norm_label":"graphify wiki index navigation","source_file":"AGENTS.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"id":"agents_graphify","label":"AGENTS.md graphify Agent Instructions","_origin":"semantic","author":null,"captured_at":null,"community":2,"community_name":"Graphify Agent Workflow","contributor":null,"file_type":"document","norm_label":"agents.md graphify agent instructions","source_file":"AGENTS.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"id":"agents_graphify_committed_graph_diff","label":"Committed graph.json Diff Expectation","_origin":"semantic","author":null,"captured_at":null,"community":2,"community_name":"Graphify Agent Workflow","contributor":null,"file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"committed graph.json diff expectation","rationale":"graphify-out/graph.json is rewritten whole on every build, so a large diff in a pull request is expected and must not be flagged as churn or used as grounds to skip the graph rebuild or its hooks.","source_file":"AGENTS.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"id":"agents_graphify_incremental_update","label":"Graphify Incremental Update After Code Changes","_origin":"semantic","author":null,"captured_at":null,"community":2,"community_name":"Graphify Agent Workflow","contributor":null,"file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"graphify incremental update after code changes","rationale":"`graphify update .` is run after modifying code because it is AST-only and incurs no API cost, keeping the graph current cheaply. Dirty graphify-out/ files are expected and are explicitly not a reason to skip graphify; skipping is only valid when the task concerns stale or incorrect graph output or the user opts out.","source_file":"AGENTS.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"id":"agents_graphify_query_first_protocol","label":"Graphify Query-First Protocol","_origin":"semantic","author":null,"captured_at":null,"community":2,"community_name":"Graphify Agent Workflow","contributor":null,"file_type":"rationale","norm_label":"graphify query-first protocol","rationale":"Agents must run `graphify query` before any grep, search, or raw source read for codebase questions, and propagate that rule into every subagent prompt. Rationale: graph queries return a scoped subgraph that is usually far smaller than GRAPH_REPORT.md or raw grep output, keeping context usage low and reads targeted.","source_file":"AGENTS.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"id":"ref_node_url","label":"ref_node_url","community":0,"community_name":"Vite Build Tooling","external":true,"file_type":"concept","norm_label":"ref_node_url","source_file":"","type":"external"}],"links":[{"source":"package","target":"ref_vue","relation":"imports","_origin":"ast","confidence":"EXTRACTED","confidence_score":1.0,"context":"import","source_file":"package.json","source_location":"L12","weight":1.0},{"source":"package","target":"ref_vitejs_plugin_vue","relation":"imports","_origin":"ast","confidence":"EXTRACTED","confidence_score":1.0,"context":"import","source_file":"package.json","source_location":"L15","weight":1.0},{"source":"package","target":"ref_vite","relation":"imports","_origin":"ast","confidence":"EXTRACTED","confidence_score":1.0,"context":"import","source_file":"package.json","source_location":"L16","weight":1.0},{"source":"package","target":"ref_vite_plugin_vue_devtools","relation":"imports","_origin":"ast","confidence":"EXTRACTED","confidence_score":1.0,"context":"import","source_file":"package.json","source_location":"L17","weight":1.0},{"source":"source_main","target":"ref_vue